# The CPU llama build, named explicitly. The repo also carries
# synapse-llama-cuda, which provides+conflicts synapse-llama — naming the one we
# want here means the ISO's dependency resolution can never fall through to the
# CUDA provider, whose libs NEED libcuda.so.1 at load and would make synapd fail
# to start on every machine without an NVIDIA driver. The GPU build is for
# installed systems (syn-install picks it when it sees the hardware), never here.
synapse-llama
synapd
synsh
synnet
synguard
synui
syn-model
syn
syn-firstboot
syn-install
synapse_kmod
nexus-chat
tepris
chibi
foot
firefox
# File manager. Pulls Qt6 + KF6 (~550MB), which is why synui ships the two
# /etc/xdg files KDE-outside-Plasma needs to actually work: menus/applications.menu
# (or every file opens the "Open With" chooser) and kdeglobals (or "Open Terminal"
# silently does nothing, KIO's fallback being a konsole we don't ship).
dolphin
gamescope
# The bar. Neither of these was on the ISO, so the live session had no bar at
# all — no clock, no tray, no network indicator — while an installed system had
# one; that was an oversight, not a decision. synui pulls waybar in as a
# dependency now, but list it explicitly: what the ISO ships should be readable
# here rather than inferred from someone else's depends. wtype is how the bar's
# SYNAPSE button asks synui to open the start menu (there is no other IPC in).
waybar
wtype

# Bluetooth. bluez is the daemon (org.bluez); bluez-utils is bluetoothctl, which
# synui does not need — it talks BlueZ over sd-bus itself (synui/src/bt.c) — but
# which is the only way to debug a radio from a shell when the panel says no.
bluez
bluez-utils
virtualbox-guest-utils
dkms
xdg-desktop-portal
xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
slurp
grim
rtkit
